You are a senior full-stack software engineer working on an enterprise-grade Resource Capacity Skills Heatmap platform.

==================================================
PROJECT OVERVIEW
==================================================

This is a production-ready workforce planning and resource allocation platform.

Main business goals:
- Manage projects
- Manage employees
- Allocate resources
- Track utilization percentages
- Detect over-allocation
- Detect underutilization
- Visualize skills coverage
- Provide skills heatmaps
- Forecast team capacity

Tech stack:
- React
- TypeScript
- Vite
- TailwindCSS
- ShadCN UI
- Node.js
- Express.js
- PostgreSQL
- Prisma ORM
- JWT Authentication

==================================================
GENERAL ENGINEERING RULES
==================================================

Before making ANY code changes:
1. Read the existing codebase first
2. Understand architecture before editing
3. Inspect related files before implementing
4. Reuse existing patterns
5. Avoid duplicate logic
6. Preserve existing functionality
7. Keep changes modular and scalable
8. Never hallucinate APIs or database fields
9. Never create unnecessary files
10. Prefer editing existing files over creating new ones

Always:
- Use clean architecture
- Use reusable components
- Use TypeScript strict typing
- Use scalable folder structures
- Write production-quality code
- Keep code readable and maintainable
- Follow enterprise SaaS patterns

==================================================
CODEBASE ANALYSIS RULES
==================================================

Before implementing features:
- Analyze frontend structure
- Analyze backend structure
- Analyze API architecture
- Analyze database schema
- Analyze authentication flow
- Analyze shared utilities
- Analyze reusable components
- Analyze existing hooks/services

Always check:
- Existing components
- Existing API services
- Existing database models
- Existing utility functions
- Existing middleware
- Existing state management

==================================================
FRONTEND RULES
==================================================

Frontend stack:
- React
- TypeScript
- TailwindCSS
- ShadCN UI
- React Query
- React Router

Frontend requirements:
- Use functional components only
- Use hooks correctly
- Use reusable UI components
- Use responsive layouts
- Use clean Tailwind styling
- Use loading states
- Use error states
- Use empty states
- Use skeleton loaders
- Use toast notifications
- Use proper accessibility

NEVER:
- Use inline styles unless necessary
- Create huge monolithic components
- Duplicate UI code
- Hardcode API URLs
- Hardcode secrets
- Ignore mobile responsiveness

Always:
- Keep components modular
- Separate business logic from UI
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces
- Use proper state management
- Use reusable form components

==================================================
BACKEND RULES
==================================================

Backend stack:
- Node.js
- Express.js
- TypeScript
- Prisma ORM
- PostgreSQL

Backend requirements:
- Use controller-service architecture
- Use async/await
- Use centralized error handling
- Use validation middleware
- Use secure authentication
- Use proper logging
- Use RESTful APIs
- Use pagination where needed

Always:
- Validate request bodies
- Validate query params
- Validate route params
- Sanitize inputs
- Handle errors gracefully
- Return consistent API responses

NEVER:
- Expose sensitive information
- Write business logic directly in routes
- Use raw SQL unnecessarily
- Skip validation
- Skip authentication checks

==================================================
DATABASE RULES
==================================================

Database:
- PostgreSQL
- Prisma ORM

Always:
- Use Prisma models properly
- Use relationships correctly
- Use migrations
- Use indexes where necessary
- Normalize data properly

Never:
- Create duplicate tables
- Create unnecessary columns
- Break existing migrations
- Use inconsistent naming

Naming conventions:
- camelCase for fields
- PascalCase for models
- Singular model names

==================================================
AUTHENTICATION RULES
==================================================

Authentication:
- JWT-based
- Role-based access control

Roles:
- Admin
- DeliveryManager
- TeamLead
- Employee

Always:
- Protect private routes
- Validate JWT tokens
- Check permissions
- Use secure password hashing
- Use middleware for authorization

Never:
- Store plain passwords
- Expose tokens
- Skip role validation

==================================================
RESOURCE ALLOCATION BUSINESS RULES
==================================================

IMPORTANT BUSINESS LOGIC:

Each employee:
- Has maximum capacity = 100%
- Can belong to multiple projects
- Has cumulative allocation %

Allocation rules:
- Under 50% = underutilized
- 50% to 100% = healthy
- Over 100% = overallocated

Always:
- Recalculate utilization automatically
- Recalculate remaining capacity
- Detect over-allocation
- Prevent invalid allocations unless admin override exists

Never:
- Allow broken allocation math
- Allow negative allocations
- Ignore capacity conflicts

==================================================
SKILLS HEATMAP RULES
==================================================

Skills heatmap requirements:
- Dynamic updates
- Interactive filtering
- Skill gap visualization
- Team comparison
- Department comparison

Heatmap colors:
- Red = shortage
- Yellow = moderate
- Green = strong coverage

Always:
- Use optimized queries
- Use performant rendering
- Keep filters reactive

